\id JON  
\h Jonah 
\toc3 JON 
\mt1 JONAH  
\c 2  
\p
\v 1 Now the Lord had commanded a great whale to swallow up Jonas: and Jonas was in the belly of the whale three days and three nights.  
\v 2 And Jonas prayed to the Lord his God out of the belly of the whale,  
\v 3 and said, I cried in my affliction to the Lord my God, and he listened to me, \add even\add* to my cry out of the belly of hell: you heard my voice.  
\v 4 You did cast me into the depths of the heart of the sea, and the floods compassed me: all your billows and your waves have passed upon me.  
\v 5 And I said, I am cast out of your presence: shall I indeed look again toward your holy temple?  
\v 6 Water was poured around me to the soul: the \f + \fr 2:6 \fl Gr. \ft last. \f* lowest deep compassed me, my head went down  
\v 7 to the clefts of the mountains; I went down into the earth, whose bars are the everlasting barriers: yet, O Lord my God, let my ruined life be restored.  
\v 8 When my soul was failing \f + \fr 2:8 \fl Gr. \ft from me. \f* me, I remembered the Lord; and may my prayer come to you into your holy temple.  
\v 9 They that observe \f + \fr 2:9 \fl Gr. \ft vain and false \+add things. \+add* \f* vanities and lies have forsaken their own mercy.  
\v 10 But I will sacrifice to you with the voice of praise and thanksgiving: all that I have vowed I will pay to you, \f + \fr 2:10 \fl Or, \ft for a thank-offering to the Lord. \f* the Lord of \add my\add* salvation.  
\v 11 And the whale was commanded by the Lord, and it cast up Jonas on the dry \add land\add*.   
